course: dictionary
lesson: 11678
title: Astonishing means amazing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Astonishing means so surprising that it is hard to believe. It is a strong word, much bigger than surprising. «The results of the test were astonishing.» The results were so surprising that the teacher could hardly believe them.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «It is astonishing that a tiny seed grows into a huge oak tree.» The words tiny seed and huge oak tree show that the growing is very surprising. Ask: would a small surprise fit here? If not, astonishing is the right word.
explain: Astonishing comes from the verb astonish, so you may also see astonished and astonishes. «Mia was astonished by the ice cave.» Astonished describes the person who feels the surprise. Astonishing describes the thing that causes it.
fact: Astonishing means so surprising that it is hard to believe; amazing.
fact: «Astonishing» is an adjective, a word that describes a noun such as a discovery or a sight.
fact: The verb «astonish» means to surprise someone very much.
fact: «Astonished» describes the person who feels surprised; «astonishing» describes the thing that causes the surprise.
fact: A quick check: swap in «amazing» or «very surprising». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «The scientists made an astonishing discovery.» What does astonishing mean? | Boring and slow | *So surprising that it is hard to believe | Wet and cold | Very small and quiet
exercise: «It is astonishing that a tiny seed grows into an oak tree.» What is astonishing here? | The soil the seed is planted in | The shape of the leaves | The colour of the seed | *The growing of a tiny seed into a huge tree
exercise: «Mia was astonished by the ice cave.» Find and copy the word that shows Mia felt surprise. | cave | *astonished | Mia | ice
test:
«The numbers in the answer were astonishing, far bigger than anyone expected.» What does astonishing show? | Ordinary, nothing special | *Something so surprising that it is hard to believe | Something that makes you sleepy | Something very quiet
test: Which word means the same as astonishing? | *Amazing | Heavy | Quick | Dull
exam: «Alice found every part of Wonderland astonishing.» Why does Alice find it astonishing? | Because it is dark there | Because she is bored | *Because everything there is so surprising that it is hard to believe | Because it is the same as home
